{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1549479-restoration-of-willpower-by-sleep","id":1549479,"title":"Restoration of Willpower by sleep","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-21T06:03:24-07:00","id":1549479,"title":"Restoration of Willpower by sleep","content":"I thought that all characters in general can restore willpower by full night sleep. Then I was watching a vampire campaign by <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@DorkTales\" target=\"_blank\">Dork Tales</a>, where the GM explicitly mentioned that vampires do not restore willpower by sleep. This surprised me, because I do not recall it would be explicitly mentioned in the rules. I searched a bit in other rulebooks, and it seems to me that it is just not mentioned, with exception of the Chronicles of Darkness core rulebook. (This could be interpreted as they cannot restore WP, because it is not explicitly allowed, or that they can, because of fallback to the core rules).<br /> <br /> Did I just search wrongly? Can you please write which supernaturals are eligible for regaining WB by sleeping? Also, where is this written? Is it in the rulebooks, or in some errata I missed?<br /> <br /> I will also say, if I were to rule right now, I would say:<br /> <br /> Mortals, Hunters, Mages, Changelings: Yes, they are still essentially human.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, Geist, Mummy, Beasts: I have no clue.<br /> <br /> Vampires, Ghosts: No, they are not really alive. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T07:11:55-07:00","id":1549480,"title":"","content":"There's a section in the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/361809/Players-Guide-to-the-Contagion-Chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle</a>, including a sidebar on page 7 that vampires not regaining Willpower from sleep was the intention. The section the sidebar is in the middle of also provides the statement that most monsters regain Willpower from getting a good night's rest, as well as a general rule that if sleep is truly restful for the creature in question and helps them connect to themselves and affirm their identity (rather than eroding it), they regain Willpower in that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T10:16:05-07:00","id":1549500,"title":"","content":"Thank you for this reference! Is there anything to how it is with the other supernaturals? How would you decide this in your game? (per supernatural)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T18:04:11-07:00","id":1549504,"title":"","content":"I have mentioned most of the statements the section makes on this topic, besides a note that officially demons recover Willpower from rest like humans do as part of an example of how one might tweak the rule for different types of monster or different individual monsters.<br /> <br /> Personally, my rationales would go as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>Demons: </b>As mentioned, while material exists suggesting it can vary from demon to demon, the default assumption is that demons have restful sleep that restores their Willpower. Given that the demonic form conveys a general lack of need for food, water, sleep, etc, and is closer to the character's angelic origins (and, for the Burned, intimates a much more stressful state of affairs), I would probably say that if for whatever reason you try to sleep in demonic form you don't recover Willpower from it for the same reason that you can't bootstrap an emotional reaction without being in Cover; this makes the Burned need to focus more on their Virtues and Vices if they want to be able to offer pacts weighted in their favor to rebuild their mortal lives.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires:</b> Requiem has a brutal resource management puzzle underpinning its human drama, most prominently in preserving Vitae you would otherwise lose healing wounds during daysleep. They have two different identity-based Anchors and at least one Touchstone to recover Willpower from, and elders likewise pick up Anachronisms to further supplement their Willpower recovery, but otherwise this is one more existential pressure for the Kindred to disappear into the shadows and leave protracted and recurring stress and violence to the layer of conspiracy that the Blood facilitates for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves:</b> Werewolves are living creatures who have souls, dream, and possess a primal connection with the vital aspects of the material world. Access to lethal stat-boosting forms notwithstanding, it would be really rough for the Uratha to be given thinner access to the resource that unspecialized violence is supposed to burn through than mortals get and pretty weird for a standard issue Glory 3 Cahalith to be deprived of one of the tools in their arsenal when hunting werewolf prey.<br /> <br /> <b>Prometheans:</b> The Created are not supposed to be here, but they are made of stuff that resonates with the world \u2014 hence the many methods of regaining Pyros that don't rely on human contact. Most prominently, the Vivid Dreams Merit (p117) that modifies the roll to recover Pyros by sleeping near one's element also doubles the amount of Willpower the character regains from sleeping a limited number of times per story.<br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eaters:</b> The presence of a krewe's Virtue and Creed as extra Anchors, coupled with the general drive of the Bound toward specific personal and institutional goals in the form of their Touchstones, mean there's similar reasons to steer them more toward that mode of behavior if you like by cutting off the most passive source of Willpower recovery, but the line has not historically done much to emphasize the bodily horror of being Bound and thereby fungibly substituted with ectoplasm; being immune to getting knocked unconscious does not prevent them from restful sleep any more than it messes with the other aspects of their biology.<br /> <br /> <b>Mortals, Mages, Changelings, Hunters, Mummies, Beasts, Deviants:</b> All of these have a mechanic in their iteration of the core rules describing Willpower (often right after the list of Common Actions and/or When To Roll Dice sections) explicitly stating they regain Willpower from rest. (Mage p213, Changeling p181, Hunter p135, Mummy p180, Beast p157, Deviant p193).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T04:56:07-07:00","id":1549522,"title":"","content":"I personally house-ruled that a Slumbering Beast has a blank dreamless sleep with no willpower regaining.<br /> That s because a Beast dream is the point of view of its roaming Horror, and if the Horror is sleeping the Beast experiences...nothing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}